      "sourceTextSha256": "7150e4097d9921ce5f195b04ffba4369fdbd50910d04cf3c3d04af33aa3fcfbe",
      "text": "After breakfast, take a tour of the old town with an English-speaking guide. Cartagena stands on the Caribbean coast, and its walled historic centre is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.\n\nThe tour takes in the 17th-century San Felipe de Barajas Fortress, old churches and well-known city landmarks. As you walk through the neighbourhoods within the old walls, you can see how Cartagena's architecture has been preserved. Then head up Cerro de la Popa to visit the monastery, which offers panoramic views across the city. Cartagena is also known for its varied cuisine. After the tour, you can continue exploring the city independently before returning to the hotel to rest.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-translator-20261110-mw9trnme-si5iwi",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      }
